Q1. What is Data?Answer: Data is a collection of unprocessed items that can include text, numbers, images, audio, and video.Q2. What is Information?Answer: Information is processed data that is organized, meaningful, and useful.Q3. What is Data Integrity?Answer: Data integrity identifies the quality of data entered into a database.Q4. What is GIGO?Answer: GIGO stands for Garbage In, Garbage Out. Incorrect data entered into a computer produces incorrect information.Q5. What is Validation?Answer: Validation is the process of comparing data with a set of rules or values to determine whether the data meets certain criteria.Q6. Write any five qualities of valuable information.Answer: Accurate, Verifiable, Timely, Organized, Accessible.Q7. Why do we study databases?Answer: Databases provide tools for storing, searching, and managing large amounts of information.Q8. What is a Database?Answer: A database is a collection of data arranged for ease and speed of search and retrieval.Q9. What is a Database System?Answer: A database system consists of data, software, hardware, and users.Q10. Write five functions of a database system.Answer: Store, Update, Retrieve, Organize, and Protect data.Q11. Who is a DBA?Answer: DBA stands for Database Administrator. A DBA designs and manages the database system.Q12. What is a DBMS?Answer: DBMS stands for Database Management System. It is software that controls the information in a database.Q13. Give examples of DBMS.Answer: Oracle, IBM DB2, MS SQL Server, MS Access, Ingres, PostgreSQL, and MySQL.Q14. What is DDL?Answer: DDL stands for Data Definition Language.Q15. What is DML?Answer: DML stands for Data Manipulation Language.Q16. What is DCL?Answer: DCL stands for Data Control Language.Q17. What is Metadata?Answer: Metadata means data about data.Q18. What is a Data Dictionary?Answer: A data dictionary stores information about the database itself, such as tables, users, rules, views, and indexes.Q19. What is a File-Based System?Answer: A file-based system stores data in individual files, where each file has a specific format.Q20. Write problems of file-based systems.Answer:No standardsData duplicationData dependenceNo ad hoc queriesLack of securityLack of recoveryLack of concurrencyPart 2 — Heavy MCQs1. Which one is processed data?A. DataB. InformationC. FileD. HardwareAnswer: B — Information2. Which of the following can be included in data?A. TextB. NumbersC. ImagesD. All of theseAnswer: D — All of these3. GIGO stands for:A. Good Input Good OutputB. Garbage In Garbage OutC. Good Information Good OutputD. Garbage Information Good OutputAnswer: B — Garbage In, Garbage Out4. Validation is used to:A. Delete dataB. Compare data with rules or valuesC. Create hardwareD. Format a computerAnswer: B5. Which information is error-free?A. TimelyB. OrganizedC. AccurateD. AccessibleAnswer: C — Accurate6. Information that can be proven correct or incorrect is:A. UsefulB. VerifiableC. TimelyD. OrganizedAnswer: B — Verifiable7. Information available when the decision maker needs it is:A. AccessibleB. AccurateC. Cost-effectiveD. OrganizedAnswer: A — Accessible8. Which is NOT a quality of valuable information?A. AccurateB. TimelyC. AccessibleD. DuplicatedAnswer: D — Duplicated9. A database is mainly used for:A. Storing and retrieving dataB. Playing gamesC. Designing hardwareD. Installing WindowsAnswer: A10. A database system consists of:A. Data onlyB. Software onlyC. Data, software, hardware and usersD. Hardware onlyAnswer: C11. Who uses the database to achieve some goal?A. End userB. DBAC. ProgrammerD. Hardware engineerAnswer: A — End user12. Who writes software to allow end users to interface with the database?A. DBAB. Application developerC. End userD. Data entry operatorAnswer: B13. Who designs and manages the database system?A. End userB. Application developerC. DBAD. CustomerAnswer: C — DBA14. DBMS stands for:A. Database Management SystemB. Data Backup Management SystemC. Database Machine SystemD. Data Management SoftwareAnswer: A15. Which one is a DBMS?A. MySQLB. PhotoshopC. PowerPointD. ChromeAnswer: A — MySQL16. Which language is used for data definition?A. DMLB. DCLC. DDLD. DBMSAnswer: C — DDL17. DML stands for:A. Data Management LanguageB. Data Manipulation LanguageC. Database Machine LanguageD. Data Mapping LanguageAnswer: B18. DCL stands for:A. Data Control LanguageB. Database Control LogicC. Data Command LanguageD. Database Coding LanguageAnswer: A19. Metadata means:A. Big dataB. Data about dataC. Deleted dataD. Duplicate dataAnswer: B20. Which stores information about database objects?A. Data dictionaryB. KeyboardC. Operating systemD. CompilerAnswer: A — Data dictionary21. Which of the following can be described by a data dictionary?A. TablesB. UsersC. IndexesD. All of theseAnswer: D22. Which is a problem of file-based systems?A. Data duplicationB. Data independenceC. Advanced securityD. Easy SQL queryingAnswer: A23. File-based systems have:A. High data redundancyB. Minimal redundancyC. Zero redundancyD. Automatic normalizationAnswer: A24. DBMS generally provides:A. Higher securityB. No securityC. Only OS-level securityD. No user controlAnswer: A25. Which system supports efficient SQL querying?A. File-based systemB. DBMSC. Manual file systemD. Paper systemAnswer: B — DBMS26. Which system supports multi-user access more easily?A. File-based systemB. DBMSC. Manual systemD. Text editorAnswer: B — DBMS27. In a file-based system, programs depend on:A. File formatB. Internet speedC. Monitor sizeD. Keyboard typeAnswer: A28. Which system provides robust backup/recovery according to the comparison?A. File-based systemB. DBMSC. Both equallyD. NeitherAnswer: B — DBMS29. Which is a major advantage of DBMS over file-based systems?A. More data duplicationB. Better security and data sharingC. More data dependenceD. No queryingAnswer: B30. Which one is NOT listed as a DBMS feature?A. PersistenceB. ConcurrencyC. SecurityD. Data destructionAnswer: D